  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Payment to EU of disallowable expenditure from BAN197/ICD840</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Following an EU audit of EIDHR/2017/391-540 (&#x2018;Empowerment of women and girl migrant workers, communities and key institutions to protect and promote migrant workers&apos; rights and access to justice&#x2019;),  19,537.23 EUR of reported expenditure was disallowed.  Of the total, 704.43 EUR is owed by CAFOD and 18,832.80 EUR owed by OKUP.     It has been agreed that CAFOD will make a payment to the EU for 100% of the amount owed.  CAFOD will support OKUP by covering part of their share through this approval (10,295.57 EUR).  OKUP will remain responsible for the balance (8,537.23 EUR) which will be recovered through deducting the amount from funds owed to OKUP under BAN236. 

CAFOD was the co-applicant and partner OKUP was the lead applicant for this EIDHR-funded project which was implemented between 2018-2021.  CAFOD provided co-funding of GBP 80,000 (BAN197/ICD840).</narrative>
  </description>
